# Finish worktree with GitHub PR

Development happens on GitHub (`siper/Mediator`). Do not use Forgejo or `fj`.

When a feature / fix / refactor / chore / docs task done in a git worktree is
ready to close out:

1. Ensure checks pass and changes are committed on the worktree branch.
2. Push the branch to GitHub: `git push -u github HEAD`
3. Create a pull request against `main` with GitHub CLI (`gh`).
   Write the PR title and body in English.

```bash
gh pr create --repo siper/Mediator --base main --title "<conventional summary>" --body "## Summary
- <what changed and why>

## Test plan
- [ ] <how to verify>"
```

4. Return the PR URL to the user.
5. Do not merge the PR unless the user explicitly asks.

Use `--fill` only when commit messages already make a clear PR title/body.
Never skip the PR step when finishing a worktree task.
